          "params": [
            {
              "name": "update",
              "type": "() => Synchronous",
              "optional": false
            }
          ],
          "returnType": "void",
          "description": "Runs update with notifications deferred: every write takes effect immediately, and subscribers are notified once, after the outermost batch completes, with the final values. ts Observable.batch(() => { player.health.value = 100; player.stats.ammo.value = 30; player.stats.level.value++; });  - Reads inside the batch see the written values; derived values compute from the current sources. - Values are delivered in the order they first changed, and each derived value after everything it depends on. A derived value recomputes once and notifies only if its result changed, so a text built from several changed values is computed and applied once. - Batches nest; only the outermost one delivers. Changes made by listeners during the delivery are delivered in the same pass. - There is no rollback. When update throws, the writes made so far stay, their notifications are delivered, and the error is rethrown. A throwing listener stops the remaining listeners of that value, as outside a batch, but every other queued value is still delivered; the first error is rethrown afterwards. - Owner notifications of vectors and sizes, such as transform invalidation, are never deferred; only their subscribers are."
        },
